<article class="env-definition" id="028D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/028D">Definition <span data-tag="028D">111.30.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $\alpha : K^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ be a morphism of complexes of $\text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. We say that $\alpha $ is a <em>filtered quasi-isomorphism</em> if for each $p \in \mathbf{Z}$ the morphism $\text{gr}^ p(K^\bullet ) \to \text{gr}^ p(L^\bullet )$ is a quasi-isomorphism. </p>
</article>